mode: "100644"
text: "# The SHOT framework — Runway as the director's tool\n\nRunway isn't the \"best clip in one click\" tool — it's the **director's tool.** You reach for it when\nyou need **control**: a specific camera move, a consistent character across shots, or to edit/restyle\nexisting footage. If you want a clean cinematic clip with native audio in one pass, that's **veo-3**.\nSHOT keeps a human directing — with consent and disclosure as the spine.\n\n## S — Set the shot (directorial brief)\n- Write like a director: **subject, camera move** (push-in, orbit, tracking), **motion**, **lighting/\n  mood**, **lens feel**, **aspect ratio**. Vague prompts waste credits.\n- Match the look to brand-profile. One shot = one idea; storyboard multi-shot pieces.\n\n## H — Hold consistency with References\n- Use **Gen-4 References** to lock a character/object/style and reuse it across every shot — Runway's\n  signature advantage. Establish the reference before generating the sequence.\n- Keep wardrobe, faces, and props consistent shot-to-shot; this is what makes AI video look produced\n  rather than random.\n\n## O — Operate the controls\n- **Camera Control** for the move (static toggle to calm motion); **Motion Brush / Multi-Motion\n  Brush** to direct motion in specific areas.\n- **Aleph (video-to-video)** to *edit existing footage* by prompt — relight, add/remove objects,\n  restyle — without regenerating. Edit-grade, fast.\n- **Act-Two** for performance capture from any camera — **consented performers only** (see spine).\n- Pick the model: **Gen-4.5** (hero), **Gen-4 Turbo** (cheap iteration), **Gen-4 Image** (stills).\n\n## T — Trim & assemble\n- Clips are **2–10s with no native audio** — so plan to **stitch shots in the edit**, add **voiceover\n  via ai-voiceover** and music/sound design in post, then **captions via captions-and-clipping.**\n- Test cheap and short, lock the storyboard, then commit credits to the high-quality hero runs.\n\n## The spine: consent + disclosure (never optional)\n- **Act-Two only on consented performers / your own performance / licensed-owned characters.** Never\n  transpose a real non-consenting person's face or performance (deepfake).\n- **Disclose** AI-generated/edited video (EU AI Act; TikTok auto; YouTube Altered-Content).\n\n## The shot brief a request should fill\n```\nSHOT: subject + camera move + motion + lighting/mood + aspect ratio\nMODEL: Gen-4.5 (hero) | Gen-4 Turbo (test) | Aleph (edit existing) | Act-Two (consented perf)\nREFERENCES: character/object/style locked across shots?\nASSEMBLE: 2-10s shots → edit; audio via ai-voiceover; captions via captions-and-clipping\nCONSENT + DISCLOSURE: confirmed\n```\n"
